# behavior-docs real-corpus recorded findings
#
# Every line below is a finding the three conformance evaluators CURRENTLY report
# against the real in-repo behavior-docs sets and pr-pool's implementation. This
# file is a RATCHET, not an exemption list: `tests/behavior-docs-real-corpus.sh`
# fails on any difference in EITHER direction, so a new finding fails the gate AND
# a fixed finding fails it too until its line is deleted here. A baseline allowed
# to keep entries for defects that no longer exist stops being a record.
#
# Format: <check-id>|<finding line, leading space stripped, runs of whitespace squeezed>
#
# Do NOT add a line to silence a finding you introduced. Fix the finding. A line
# belongs here only when the fix is real work with a real owner, named below.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. pr-pool has PARTIALLY adopted INV-22 (13 lines)
#
# All 13 of pr-pool's stories carry a per-element listing; none of its 1 journey and
# 12 use cases do. INV-22 makes the listing a per-element obligation, so this is a
# genuine violation of a rule the method set already ships. It is PARTIAL adoption,
# which is the state the check is sharpest about: a set with zero listings has simply
# not been retrofitted yet, whereas a set with some listings has adopted the rule and
# the gaps are omissions. Owner: the pr-pool set retrofit (WS-2/3/4 of the six-set
# restructure), not this work stream.
#
# The names below are NOT the ten `JOURNEY-*` this section first recorded. The
# journey rebuild (bead pg2-wr6lm.5.8) re-shaped and retyped the set onto an
# enumerated lifecycle-action matrix, so seven of those ten lines were UPDATED to the
# renamed element rather than deleted (the finding is the same omission on the same
# element under a new name), two were deleted because the element they named was
# folded away, and five were added for elements the rebuild created. `JOURNEY-FLOW`
# is the one name that did not change: it is now the set's single summary-level
# journey. So the ten split 7 renamed + 1 unchanged + 2 folded away, and net
# 10 -> 13 lines, all of them the same unretrofitted-listing defect with the same
# owner.
#
# 2. Prose references that resolve to nothing (2 lines, both WARN)
#
# `INV-DISP-1` and `INTF-SOURCE` in the METHOD set are ID-shaped literals printed
# to ILLUSTRATE the namespacing convention, not citations of elements — the root
# method cites no other set and its imports table is deliberately empty. They are
# recorded rather than fixed because no grep distinguishes a style example from a
# citation, and a reader cannot either, which is itself worth a decision.
#
# Both of those lines carry `file:line` coordinates — and they are the ONLY finding
# lines here that do — so ANY insertion above them in the named file MOVES them and
# the baseline line must be re-recorded. That is a location change, not a new or fixed
# finding — re-run the runner and copy the new coordinates. If a future finding line
# carries coordinates too, this count is stale: re-derive it rather than trust it.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
